# condor_submit_dag sweep_45_dumusque_mu_rawccf.dag : the plage part of sweep_45_dumusque_mu.dag (A_th, parameters.txt)
# again with ccf_norm = 2 (CCF_NORM of settings_45_dumusque_mu.sh, set in the .sub files: raw ring CCFs, the brightness
# of the spots and faculae and the limb darkening in the RV) and the Dumusque bisector times mu (dumusque_mu_scaling =
# 0, 1). The identification and the filling factors are those of sweep_4096.dag; the confs, grids, sets, opt_rv and
# results go to the folders with the suffix _rawccf in ${BASE}/dumusque_mu:
#   1. the grids once per T_sp of parameters.txt (build_grids_45_dumusque_mu_rawccf.sub)
#   2. one simulation per line of parameters.txt (run_opt_rv_45_dumusque_mu_rawccf_plage.sub)
#   3. table of all the sets and the figures (collect_stats_45_dumusque_mu_rawccf.sub; it runs even if some sets failed)
JOB grids          build_grids_45_dumusque_mu_rawccf.sub
JOB sets_plage     run_opt_rv_45_dumusque_mu_rawccf_plage.sub
JOB collect_plage  collect_stats_45_dumusque_mu_rawccf.sub
VARS collect_plage   kind="plage"
PARENT grids CHILD sets_plage
PARENT sets_plage CHILD collect_plage
SCRIPT POST sets_plage  /bin/true
